WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.540
Every writer knows this page.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.300
The blank one.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.680
The one that waits.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.000
Twyne doesn't start you here.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.340
It starts you from a brief: a ten-minute

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.720
interview that every tool in the room reads.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.380
And the room is full.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.840
Five editors read every draft against your brief.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.780
A sceptic for your argument.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.060
A patron for what's already working.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.200
A scholar for your evidence.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.920
A copy chief for every sentence.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.640
And the reader you're actually writing for.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.360
A rubric grades you on the target.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.820
Not on how fluent you sound.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.500
Your draft stays on your desk, until you

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.160
decide it goes anywhere else.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:50.420
Twyne.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.360
Draft with a room full of editors.
